<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong to hold textile talks with Washington.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong to hold textile talks with Washington.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong officials will go to Washington for consultations about on-going textile issues to be held next Monday, the government said on Friday.</p>
<p>The Hong Kong team will be led by the deputy-director general of trade, Rebecca Lai.</p>
<p>The matters to be discussed include Washington's decision in 1995 to use its import data instead of Hong Kong's export data for quota accounting purposes, and changes in U.S. origin rules which took effect last year.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
